This extension uses the publicly known approach of replacing ad-containing HLS playlists
with a playlist requested for another player type, as popularised by open source projects
such as TwitchAdSolutions (MIT). No code from GPL-licensed projects is included.

Version 1.1.0 (mid-roll handling, worker injection by fetching the worker script and
prepending the hook, multiple playerType/platform backups) follows ideas described by
TwitchAdSolutions (pixeltris, MIT) and TTV-AB (GosuDRM). The code is written independently;
no source code from these projects is included.

Version 1.2.0 recognises the current usher endpoint (/api/v2/channel/hls/) and adds debug
logging; injection now happens before the first navigation of a tab. Independent code.

Version 1.3.0 adapts logic from the following projects (rewritten, not copied verbatim):
- TwitchAdSolutions / vaft by pixeltris, MIT License,
  https://github.com/pixeltris/TwitchAdSolutions
  (PlaybackAccessToken persisted query and platform choice, backup player type order with
  embed fallback, relaying GQL requests from the player worker through the page with the
  page's Client-Integrity / Authorization / Device / Client-Version / Session headers,
  forcing the page's own token to playerType "popout", removing parent_domains from the usher
  URL, dropping prefetch hints during ads, reloading the player via setSrc after an ad).
- TTV-AB by GosuDRM, MIT-based license with repository attribution,
  Copyright (c) 2025 GosuDRM, https://github.com/GosuDRM/TTV-AB
  (player type candidates site/embed/popout/mobile_web/autoplay, reuse of the page's
  persisted-query hash, retry cooldown for backups that carry ads).
